{% comment %}
  Contact details + form, in one card that overlaps the band above.

  THE FORM IS REAL. The mockup's is a dead <button type="button">; this uses
  Shopify's {% form 'contact' %}. It posts to the store and Shopify sends the
  mail itself, to SETTINGS > GENERAL > STORE CONTACT DETAILS > STORE EMAIL
  (shop.email) -- established by test, not by the docs. Not Sender email, which
  is a different field under Notifications and only sets the From address on
  customer-facing mail.

  Nothing here needs an app and there is no JavaScript for the submit: Shopify
  redirects back with ?contact_posted=true, which drives the success message.

  That redirect is also why the success note carries tabindex="-1" and is
  focused on load -- after a full page reload a screen reader user would
  otherwise be returned to the top of the document with no indication that
  anything happened.

  Contact details are blocks so a merchant can add or drop a line (hours, a
  second location) without a developer.

  ELEMENT. The root is a <div>: the schema's `"tag": "section"` already wraps
  this in <section id="shopify-section-...">.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign classes = 'suf-section'
  if section.settings.overlap
    assign classes = classes | append: ' suf-section--overlap-up'
  endif
-%}

<div class="{{ classes }}">
  <div class="suf-wrap">
    <div class="suf-contact-card">
      <div class="suf-contact-split">
        <div class="suf-contact-info">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.settings.label != blank and block.settings.value != blank -%}
              <div class="suf-cblock" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <h4>{{ block.settings.label | escape }}</h4>
                <p>
                  {%- liquid
                    assign target = block.settings.link_value | default: block.settings.value
                    assign tel = target | remove: ' ' | remove: '(' | remove: ')' | remove: '-' | remove: '.'
                  -%}
                  {%- case block.settings.link_as -%}
                    {%- when 'tel' -%}
                      <a href="tel:{{ tel }}">{{ block.settings.value | escape }}</a>
                    {%- when 'email' -%}
                      <a href="mailto:{{ target | escape }}">{{ block.settings.value | escape }}</a>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{ block.settings.value | escape | newline_to_br }}
                  {%- endcase -%}
                </p>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>

        <div class="suf-contact-form">
          {%- comment -%}
            Always rendered, visible only once the columns stack.

            Side by side, the form needs no label: it sits beside the contact
            details and is obviously the other half of the pair. Stacked, the
            first field arrives straight after the address with nothing to say
            a form has started.

            It is not hidden with display:none above the breakpoint but
            visually hidden, so it stays in the accessibility tree at every
            width -- a heading before a form is worth more to someone
            navigating by headings than it is to someone who can see the
            layout.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if section.settings.form_heading != blank -%}
            <h2 class="suf-contact-form__head">{{ section.settings.form_heading | escape }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- form 'contact', class: 'suf-cform' -%}
            {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
              <p class="suf-form-note suf-form-note--success" tabindex="-1" data-suf-form-success>
                {{ section.settings.success_message | default: 'Thanks -- your message is on its way. We usually reply the same day.' }}
              </p>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if form.errors -%}
              <div class="suf-form-note suf-form-note--error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" data-suf-form-success>
                <strong>That didn't send.</strong>
                <ul>
                  {%- for field in form.errors -%}
                    <li>
                      {%- if field == 'form' -%}
                        {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}
                      {%- else -%}
                        {{ form.errors.translated_fields[field] | capitalize }}
                        {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="suf-cform__row">
              <div class="suf-field">
                <label for="suf-cf-name">Name</label>
                <input
                  type="text"
                  id="suf-cf-name"
                  name="contact[name]"
                  autocomplete="name"
                  value="{{ form.name }}"
                  required
                >
              </div>
              <div class="suf-field">
                <label for="suf-cf-email">Email</label>
                <input
                  type="email"
                  id="suf-cf-email"
                  name="contact[email]"
                  autocomplete="email"
                  value="{{ form.email }}"
                  required
                >
              </div>
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              A REASON, FOR TRIAGE. The visitor gains nothing -- they know why
              they are writing. It exists so "I want to get certified" and "my
              order never arrived" stop landing in one undifferentiated pile,
              since those need different people and different urgency.

              So every option has to change what the merchant DOES. "Feedback"
              and "feature request" both resolve to "read when there is time",
              which is one behaviour, and two labels for one behaviour just
              makes the list longer to read.

              NOT REQUIRED. Shopify drops a blank value rather than sending an
              empty line, so leaving it alone costs nothing.

              `contact[Reason]` is capitalised because the key is the label
              Shopify prints in the email.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign reasons = section.settings.reasons | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
            {%- if reasons.size > 0 -%}
              <div class="suf-field">
                <label for="suf-cf-reason">{{ section.settings.reason_label | default: "What's this about?" | escape }}</label>
                <select id="suf-cf-reason" name="contact[Reason]">
                  <option value="">Choose one</option>
                  {%- for reason in reasons -%}
                    {%- assign clean = reason | strip -%}
                    {%- if clean != blank -%}
                      <option value="{{ clean | escape }}">{{ clean }}</option>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="suf-field">
              <label for="suf-cf-message">Message</label>
              <textarea id="suf-cf-message" name="contact[body]" rows="6" required>{{ form.body }}</textarea>
            </div>

            <button type="submit" class="suf-btn suf-btn--primary">
              {{- section.settings.submit_label | default: 'Send Message' | escape -}}
            </button>
          {%- endform -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Contact card (SUF)",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "overlap",
      "label": "Overlap the band above",
      "info": "Only turn this on when the section directly above is a Page band with its overlap setting on.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "form_heading",
      "label": "Heading above the form",
      "info": "Shown once the columns stack; read by screen readers at every width.",
      "default": "Send a Message"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "reason_label",
      "label": "Reason field label",
      "default": "What's this about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "reasons",
      "label": "Reasons",
      "info": "One per line, and they arrive on the email as \"Reason: ...\". Keep the list to four or five: every option should change what YOU do when it arrives, or it is a label for its own sake. Leave empty to drop the field.",
      "default": "I'm interested in getting certified\nQuestion about a seminar\nQuestion about my order\nSomething else"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "submit_label",
      "label": "Submit button label",
      "default": "Send Message"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "success_message",
      "label": "Message shown after sending",
      "default": "Thanks -- your message is on its way. We usually reply the same day."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "detail",
      "name": "Contact detail",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Label",
          "info": "Phone, Email, Address, Hours."
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "value",
          "label": "Value",
          "info": "Line breaks are preserved."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "link_value",
          "label": "Link target (optional)",
          "info": "Use when the link must differ from the visible text -- e.g. show \"(000) 000-0000\" but dial \"+1 000 000 0000\". Leave blank to derive it from the value."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "link_as",
          "label": "Make this a link",
          "options": [
            { "value": "none", "label": "Plain text" },
            { "value": "tel", "label": "Phone number" },
            { "value": "email", "label": "Email address" }
          ],
          "default": "none"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Contact card (SUF)",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "detail" }, { "type": "detail" }, { "type": "detail" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
